  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Planning &amp; architecture</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Right-sized designs from requirements.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>We begin by defining business, technical, and regulatory requirements, then translate them into practical infrastructure specifications. This includes capacity planning, redundancy strategies, space layout, and technology selections aligned with proven industry standards.</p>
          <p>Our focus is on right-sized designs: we evaluate load profiles, growth projections, and risk tolerance to avoid oversizing power, cooling, and IT systems. The result is an infrastructure that meets availability targets while remaining cost-effective and maintainable over time. Over-engineered, oversized designs that increase cost without improving resilience are avoided by design.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section-alt reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">High availability</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Availability by design, not by duplication.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>High availability is achieved through careful architecture, not just hardware duplication. We design multi-path power and cooling, fault-tolerant network topologies, and maintenance-friendly layouts that minimise single points of failure and reduce both planned and unplanned downtime.</p>
          <p>Our approach accounts for maintenance windows, failure scenarios, and operational constraints. This allows organisations to operate continuously while performing upgrades or repairs, supporting business-critical workloads without disruption. When a component needs maintenance, the system continues — that is the definition of resilient architecture.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

